    "body": "What is the `select`'s button? Isn't it the `select` element itself, which has the `appearance: menulist-button` style in the the drop-down box state? I'm trying to understand if this is different from \"the width necessary to render the widest option element in the element's list of options (including its indent, if any)\" or if maybe something could be added to the parenthetical? If it's about the little arrow, maybe the parenthetical could be \"including its indent and surrounding UI, if any\"?\r\n\r\nNote to other reviewers: `<code>option</code>s` looked a bit unusual to me at first, but the style is widespread, especially `<code>iframe</code>s` and `<code>label</code>s`.",
